  "title": "Job 16",
  "display_title": "Job 16",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 16,
  "sortOrder": 18016,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I have heard many such things: miserable comforters are ye all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Shall vain words have an end? or what emboldeneth thee that thou answerest?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I also could speak as ye do: if your soul were in my soul’s stead, I could heap up words against you, and shake mine head at you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But I would strengthen you with my mouth, and the moving of my lips should asswage your grief.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Though I speak, my grief is not asswaged: and though I forbear, what am I eased?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And thou hast filled me with wrinkles, which is a witness against me: and my leanness rising up in me beareth witness to my face.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He teareth me in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth; mine enemy sharpeneth his eyes upon me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully; they have gathered themselves together against me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken me by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and defiled my horn in the dust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "My face is foul with weeping, and on my eyelids is the shadow of death;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Not for any injustice in mine hands: also my prayer is pure.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Also now, behold, my witness is in heaven, and my record is on high.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "My friends scorn me: but mine eye poureth out tears unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "O that one might plead for a man with God, as a man pleadeth for his neighbour!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:16:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "When a few years are come, then I shall go the way whence I shall not return.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 16:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:16:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
